/* Bottom navigation — restyled to the V2 dark bar.
 * Spec: DESIGN_IMPLEMENTATION.md §4 "Bar spec"; token mapping: Appendix A.1.
 * Figma: `Pinned Bottom Navigation` 390x98 on every V2 frame (node 29:2154 et al).
 *
 * NOTE: no hex literals anywhere in this file, comments included —
 * TokenDisciplineTests.ComponentUss_HasNoHardcodedColors scans the raw text.
 *
 * GEOMETRY (transcribed literally — 1 USS px = 1 dp = 1 Figma pt, §1.2)
 *   container   inverse-surface fill, 1px primary (navy) top border
 *   tab row     390x64, horizontal, space-between, padding 0 24
 *   tab         64 wide, vertical, gap 4, centered
 *   active      56x32 pill, padding 4/16, radius 16, secondary (amber) fill,
 *               24dp icon tinted on-secondary (navy), label 600 11px white
 *   inactive    no pill, icon + label white at 50%, label 500 11px
 *
 * The 34dp OS home-indicator strip under the row is SAFE-AREA PADDING APPLIED BY THE
 * HOST, not a drawn element (§1, Appendix B). That is why the bar declares
 * `min-height` (a floor) rather than `height`, and why the 64dp row height lives on
 * the ITEM: a host `padding-bottom: 34px` then adds below a row that stays 64 tall,
 * giving the 98dp total, instead of squeezing the row inside a fixed box.
 *
 * WHY THE BASE RULES ARE THE *INACTIVE* LOOK
 *  USS has no `:not()`, so "inactive" cannot be selected directly. The base rules
 *  therefore describe the inactive destination and `--active` overrides it. This is
 *  also where `Inter-Medium.asset` (weight 500) earns its keep: V2's inactive labels
 *  are 500 while the shared `.md-typescale-label-small` class is 600, so the 500 face
 *  is applied here, on the inactive state only, and `--active` restores the 600 face.
 *  Sizes/tracking still match label-small (11px / ls 0) — same values, different face.
 *
 * WHITE AT 50% IS NOT A LITERAL
 *  `color: var(--md-sys-color-inverse-on-surface)` + `opacity: 0.5` (Appendix A.1 maps
 *  "white at 50%" to inverse-on-surface at 50%). `opacity` is a number, not a color,
 *  so TokenDisciplineTests stays green and a re-theme still moves it.
 *
 * ONE DELIBERATE DEVIATION: THE PILL BOX IS UNCONDITIONAL
 *  V2's tabs are 41dp (inactive) and 49dp (active) tall, both centred in the 64dp row,
 *  so its inactive labels sit ~4dp HIGHER than the active one. Here the 56x32 box is
 *  always present and only its fill changes, which:
 *    - keeps every icon centre exactly where V2 puts it (23.5dp down the row, identical
 *      in both designs — the deviation is only that inactive labels join the active
 *      one's baseline instead of floating 4dp above it);
 *    - keeps the active/inactive switch a pure repaint, with no layout jump under the
 *      background-color transition;
 *    - keeps the state layer's rounded, clipped host alive for inactive presses;
 *    - avoids clipping the glyph: TextCore's line box for a 24px font is taller than
 *      24px, so a 24x24 `overflow: hidden` host would crop it.
 */

.md-nav-bar {
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 64px;
    padding-top: 0;
    padding-bottom: 0;
    padding-left: 24px;
    padding-right: 24px;
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-inverse-surface);
    border-top-width: 1px;
    border-top-color: var(--md-sys-color-primary);
}

/* One destination. Fixed 64dp width + space-between is what makes 3, 4 or 5
 * destinations all lay out without touching this file (5 x 64 = 320 <= 342dp of
 * content width at 390dp). `flex-shrink: 0` keeps that true at the 5-tab end. */
.md-nav-bar__item {
    width: 64px;
    height: 64px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
}

/* Icon host — the active-indicator pill: 56x32, padding 4/16 around the 24dp icon.
 * Transparent when inactive (V2: "no pill"), amber when active; see the deviation
 * note in the header for why the BOX is unconditional and only the fill moves. */
.md-nav-bar__indicator {
    width: 56px;
    height: 32px;
    padding: 4px 16px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    border-radius: var(--md-sys-shape-corner-large);
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    overflow: hidden;
    transition-property: background-color;
    transition-duration: var(--md-sys-motion-duration-short2);
}

.md-nav-bar__indicator .md-state-layer {
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-inverse-on-surface);
}

.md-nav-bar__icon {
    font-size: 24px;
    color: var(--md-sys-color-inverse-on-surface);
    opacity: 0.5;
}

/* Label — label-small metrics (11px / ls 0) at the 500 face (inactive).
 * `margin-top: 4px` is V2's `gap: 4`; USS has no `gap`.
 * Deliberately NOT clipped: V2 lets a long label ("Avistamentos", 72dp) overflow the
 * 64dp tab symmetrically rather than ellipsize it, and space-between leaves room. */
.md-nav-bar__label {
    margin-top: 4px;
    padding: 0;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    -unity-font-definition: url("/Assets/DesignSystem/Fonts/Inter-Medium.asset");
    color: var(--md-sys-color-inverse-on-surface);
    opacity: 0.5;
    white-space: nowrap;
}

/* ---- Active destination ---- */

.md-nav-bar__item--active .md-nav-bar__indicator {
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-secondary);
}
.md-nav-bar__item--active .md-nav-bar__icon {
    color: var(--md-sys-color-on-secondary);
    opacity: 1;
}
.md-nav-bar__item--active .md-nav-bar__label {
    -unity-font-definition: url("/Assets/DesignSystem/Fonts/Inter-SemiBold.asset");
    opacity: 1;
}
/* Ripple on the amber pill must be the on-color, not white. */
.md-nav-bar__item--active .md-state-layer {
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-on-secondary);
}

/* ---- Interaction states ---- */

.md-nav-bar__item:hover .md-state-layer {
    opacity: var(--md-sys-state-hover-opacity);
}
.md-nav-bar__item:focus .md-state-layer {
    opacity: var(--md-sys-state-focus-opacity);
}
.md-nav-bar__item:active .md-state-layer {
    opacity: var(--md-sys-state-pressed-opacity);
}
